{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{% set output_format_description = "a brief, objective observation (2-3 sentences) focused solely on the primary trend or key finding from the 'Top CWEs: Attack Vector vs. CVSS Score' chart data. No interpretation or recommendations." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
The chart titled '{{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Top CWEs: Attack Vector vs. CVSS Score') }}' (e.g., a scatter plot or bubble chart) likely displays prominent Common Weakness Enumerations (CWEs) mapped against their common Attack Vectors and typical CVSS scores.
Based *only* on the data table provided:
- Identify any prominent CWEs that consistently show high CVSS scores across different Attack Vectors.
- Note if certain Attack Vectors tend to have higher or lower CVSS scores for the CWEs listed.
- Do certain CWEs appear across multiple Attack Vectors but with varying CVSS scores?
- Are there any outlier CWEs that have an unusually high CVSS score for their typical Attack Vector?
Focus only on what the data directly indicates about the relationship between CWEs, Attack Vectors, and CVSS scores.
The following data structure contains the details of the CWE data:
CWE_DETAILS = {{ CWE_DETAILS | tojson(indent=4) }}
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Chart ID: {{ data_context_payload.chart_id | default('top_cwe_av_cvss_chart') }}
Chart Caption: {{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Figure 11. Top CWEs: Attack Vector vs. CVSS Score.') }}

Data Summary:
{{ data_context_payload.chart_data_summary | default("Data not available.") }}
